// Require a hardware login within 15 minutes before token exchange.
//
// Exchange is how workload-identity and agent credentials are obtained, and
// it presents an existing token rather than a fresh hardware touch. This
// forces a recent human authentication for those credentials, independent
// of the session's own lifetime.
//
// Gating exchange rather than login is deliberate: the FIDO2 grant is
// itself a hardware login, so this condition would always hold there.
//
// A browser enrollment also records a successful login, and enrollment is
// not posture-checked — so this proves recency, not device compliance.
@id("token_exchange_step_up")
forbid (principal, action == Vouch::Action::"ExchangeToken", resource)
when temporal {
    !(formerly within 15m Vouch::Action::"Login"::response{ output.result: true })
};
